{"kind":"request","text":"Stop the merge step from manufacturing staleness on every completed loop. AGENTS.md step 5 requires the merge to supersede the branch artifact for the path. The ready report and the approval both cite that branch artifact, correctly, because it is what they were about. So the prescribed merge retires a basis that two immutable statements name, and both go stale, and the commitment ends satisfied-and-stale. Measured at depth 2141: 62 of 89 satisfied-and-stale commitments are stale for exactly this reason, which means the projection marks most correctly finished work as needing attention and the signal loses its meaning. The distinction the fold is missing is between an artifact retired because it was wrong and an artifact superseded because its own successor now describes the same path. A review that approved an immutable head is not made untrue by that head merging. Discovered while repairing the connectors note closure under request 9b9ff10c, where the per-chain repair provably cannot fix the commitment because a report is immutable.","body":{"conditions":"The fold distinguishes supersession by a successor at the same path from retirement for wrongness, and stops propagating staleness through the first kind when the citing statement names an immutable head that did not change. Concretely: a ready report or approval that cites a pre-merge candidate artifact does not become stale merely because the merge superseded that artifact with its own merge artifact for the same path; retirement for wrongness still propagates as today. A test pins both directions: superseding a branch artifact by its merge artifact leaves the approval and the commitment non-stale, and retiring an artifact as wrong still makes them stale. The measured population is repaired by recomputation, not by rewriting history: the 62 affected commitments project satisfied without the stale qualifier after the change, verified by count before and after. ProfileVersion advances, and docs/concepts/staleness.md plus docs/reference/gs/status.md state the distinction.","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}